6.16 Practical modeling workflow
A sound SVM workflow includes:

split the data into training and test sets;
place preprocessing and SVM estimation in one pipeline;
standardize numerical variables;
select a kernel according to the expected boundary complexity;
tune C, and for RBF models tune gamma;
use cross-validation for model selection;
evaluate the final model once on untouched test data;
inspect class imbalance and choose suitable metrics.

Example pipeline:

svm_pipeline = make_pipeline(
    StandardScaler(),
    SVC(
        kernel="rbf",
        C=1,
        gamma="scale"
    )
)

